 "text": "Now stretch that out over years. Over the long run, too much sitting is linked to type two diabetes, heart disease, certain cancers... and dying earlier. One big analysis found that sitting more than eight hours a day, with no physical activity, carried a risk of death similar to obesity and smoking. And a twenty twenty-five heart study found the risk was especially high for people sitting more than about ten and a half hours a day. Think about it. A long shift. Plus dinner. Plus the couch at night. That adds up fast.",
